      <h2 id="how-we-chose">How We Chose</h2>
      <p>Every model here had to pass the same six checks. ANC class and the type of noise it targets; microphone quality for video calls; weight and clamp force, because comfort decides whether you keep wearing them; rated battery with ANC on; whether two devices can be connected at once; and list price against what the rest of the field offers at that price.</p>

      <p>Two things are deliberately excluded from the ranking. First, sound quality carries less weight than call quality, because this is a work guide: a headphone that sounds wonderful but makes you sound distant on a call fails the job. Second, we do not rank by attenuation in decibels. Vendors publish attenuation curves on different bases and rarely under the same conditions, so a single dB figure would suggest a measurement we did not make.</p>

